      <h2>Anatomy of a Classic Dairy Queen Cake</h2>
      <p>Before choosing a size, it helps to understand how a classic DQ cake is constructed from the base up. Unlike grocery store ice cream cakes that rely on sponge cake fillers, a traditional Dairy Queen cake is 100% frozen dessert:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Base Layer:</strong> Rich, velvety chocolate soft serve.</li>
        <li><strong>The Sacred Center:</strong> A thick layer of rich chocolate cold fudge surrounded by signature chocolate cookie crunch crumbles.</li>
        <li><strong>Top Layer:</strong> Smooth vanilla soft serve frosted with whipped dessert icing and personalized decorating gel.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Standard Cakes vs. Blizzard® Cakes: What's the Difference?</h2>
      <p>Dairy Queen offers two distinct styles of frozen cakes:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Classic DQ Cake:</strong> Features the traditional vanilla top, chocolate bottom, and middle fudge crunch layer. Perfect for crowd-pleasing occasions where guests have varied dessert tastes.</li>
        <li><strong>Blizzard® Cake:</strong> Replaces the plain vanilla top layer with your favorite blended Blizzard flavor (such as <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo®</a>, <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough</a>, or <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's®</a>). The iconic chocolate fudge and crunch center is still preserved in the middle! Expect to pay $3.00 to $5.00 more for a Blizzard cake compared to a standard cake.</li>
      </ol>

