      <h2>How and When to Order: Lead Times</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Need a Cake Right Now? (Grab &amp; Go Case):</strong> Almost every DQ Grill &amp; Chill location keeps 5 to 15 pre-made 8-inch and 10-inch cakes in the front display freezer. You can walk in, choose a design, and ask the decorator to write a name and message in colored icing on the spot for free in under 5 minutes.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom Design / Photo Cakes:</strong> If you want a specific Blizzard flavor, custom theme, edible photo image, or specialty piping, order at least <strong>24 to 48 hours in advance</strong> directly via DQcakes.com or by calling your local store.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Critical Cake Handling &amp; Slicing Secrets</h2>
      <p>Dairy Queen soft serve is kept in commercial blast freezers at -10°F to -15°F. To ensure your guests get clean, neat slices instead of cracked chunks, follow this timeline:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Transporting Home:</strong> Keep the cake box flat on the floorboard of your car with the AC blasting on maximum. Never put an ice cream cake on an inclined car seat!</li>
        <li><strong>The 15-Minute Tempering Rule:</strong> Take the cake out of your home freezer exactly 15 to 20 minutes before serving. Letting the frosting and outer soft serve temper slightly at room temperature makes cutting effortless.</li>
        <li><strong>The Hot Water Knife Trick:</strong> Fill a tall cup with steaming hot water. Dip your chef's knife into the hot water, wipe it dry with a paper towel, and make your first downward cut. Repeat the hot water dip between every slice for picture-perfect bakery cuts!</li>
      </ol>

